 thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found the section you're referring to. I had read it and then forgot about it. I think it's definitely an interesting take on the cyclical Gehenna myth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T10:57:46-07:00","id":1450699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447032-question-on-the-children-of-the-outer-dark-baali-lore?p=1447164#post1447164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Unknown: </b>No idea what this guy or girl was doing and it might be Ur-Shulgi.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think its been fairly explicit that Ur-Shulgi was embraced as a sleeper agent to fight the Baali, so he must postdate their origin. And got turned. Might have been the first Shaitan though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447032-question-on-the-children-of-the-outer-dark-baali-lore?p=1450470#post1450470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which, on its own has some interesting implications in the V20/Revised canon where some of the thinbloods are \u201cInceptors\u201d... vampires who created their own disciplines... something previously believed exclusive only to the Antediluvians.<br /> <br /> Except, if the Antediluvians were once thinblooded themselves and that was the point in time when they were creating their new disciplines... then there\u2019s a link. No one\u2019s been able to do much with disciplines because the general prohibitions against thinblooded progeny kept the blood too thick (one might say \u201ctoo static\u201d) to have the flexibility needed to incept new disciplines.<br /> <br /> And it could have literally been a long con by the Antediluvians to keep anyone else from being able to incept new abilities that could challenge them in ways their current stasis would prevent them from being able to adapt to.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re running with cyclical Gehennas it could even be the blood getting too thin and new disciplines being incepted that causes the Antediluvians to stir because they need to wipe out the potential threat.<br /> <br /> Take it one step further with the thickening blood and the option that the Antediluvians are NOT as powerful as they pretend to be suggesting that there could be a \u201cmax blood potency\u201d for vampires that they\u2019d all eventually reach if they live long enough and it\u2019s entirely possible that some Antediluvians meet final death in each Gehenna cycle only to have a younger inceptor replace them (and by the time the next Gehenna cycle rolls around in a few thousand years their blood has now reached \u201cmax potency\u201d).<br /> <br /> Basically, Generation only matters for those who haven\u2019t yet reached the thickness of blood where max potency caps things. Caine, the \u201cSecond\u201d and \u201cThird\u201d Generations are all said to be equally strong. But if the \u201cSecond\u201d was actually the 22nd Generation (making what we call the 12th Generation actually the 32nd) and there was still a 12th Generation Vampire around they\u2019d both be equal in power since they\u2019re both at max potency...<br /> <br /> ... and from the point of view of a \u201c5th/25th Gen\u201d sired 5000 years after that... would they even be able to tell the difference? They\u2019re all Blood Gods powerful beyond comprehension and so in stories the \u201cactive\u201d ones when things finally get written down are labeled as the 3rd Generation while those dead or in permanent torpor are labeled the 2nd Generation and their distant progenitor as Caine/the First Generation (which also fits a lot of human psychology in general... we really like the number three and dividing into thirds for some reason and it turns up in myths and stories a lot more than you\u2019d expect for a bilaterally symmetrical species with five digits on each of their four limbs).</div> </div> </div> </div>Its an interesting notion, but leaves us with Antediluvian kindred with no masquerade back through the ice age. What if the &quot;platau&quot; the &quot;max blood potency&quot; is not static, but depends on a natural predator/prey balance?<br /> <br /> So the more human blood there is in the world, the higher the max potency.<br /> <br /> Most kindred through history stayed relatively thin-blooded. But then humans invented agriculture and started building cities... &quot;Caine&quot; was the local Apex predator where agriculture took off, and with his increased blood level he and his brood wiped out the competing variants of hemivore in an increasingly wide area. Today they are remembered as legends of Lilith, Kuei-Jin, Drowned etc. And then as human population increases, max discipline level creeps upwards...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T18:39:21-07:00","id":1451598,"title":"","content":"I'm currently reading Ray Jenkins' &quot;Clanbook: Baali&quot; (available at Storytellers' Vault), and have been struck by how neatly the author ties together lore from several game editions into one tidy package. It's very clever.<br /> <br /> Jenkins frames the Children of the Outer Dark as entities that lived in the Void before Creation, which definitely lends itself to a reading as them being Neverborn Malfeans if you want them to be something that's known to exist in other game lines.<br /> <br /> The author takes care to repeatedly emphasize that the Children are definitely not demons from Hell, and that the First Tribe did not worship demons. They worshipped the Children, and their dealings with demons were for power to either wake the Children or keep them asleep. In the modern nights, the more conservative Molochim stick to the old ways, while the clan's demon worshipping bad apples are descendants of Nergal or the Other who have wandered off the path through centuries of bad leadership, careless siring, and shoddy scholarship.<br /> <br /> In this model, and in a chronicle that uses concepts from Demon: the Fallen, the Baali would have had plenty of contact with the Earthbound over the eons, but only because the Baali were summoning and exploiting the Earthbound for power to either wake or keep asleep the true objects of their worship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 06-10-2021, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}